Relevant columns, their content and why we need them  
• `date` (or the special macro `_TABLE_SUFFIX`) : to know the day – lets us group by month (Jan‑Mar 2017).  
• `hits` (REPEATED RECORD) : holds one row per hit inside every session.  
• `hits.eCommerceAction.action_type` : tells us what the user did in that hit.  
  2 = product‑detail view (denominator)  
  3 = add‑to‑cart (numerator 1)  
  6 = completed purchase (numerator 2)  
• `hits.product.isImpression` : if TRUE it is just a product‑list impression; leaving it FALSE/NULL keeps only “real” actions.  
• `fullVisitorId`, `visitId`, `sessionId …` – could be used when we need per‑user / per‑session aggregates, but not strictly needed for this task.  

Typical filters you will see below  
 WHERE h.eCommerceAction.action_type = '2'   -- product details  
 AND  (h.product.isImpression IS NULL OR h.product.isImpression = FALSE)    
 WHERE _TABLE_SUFFIX BETWEEN '20170101' AND '20170331'   -- only Jan‑Mar 2017  

--------------------------------------------------
10 exploration → answer queries (all limited to 20 rows, back‑quoted identifiers are real)

```sql
-- 1. Look at any hit on 27‑Jan‑2017
-- Description: dump a few raw hit records to understand the fields we will use.
SELECT
  h.hitNumber,
  h.time,
  h.type,
  h.eCommerceAction.action_type AS action_type,
  h.product.isImpression AS isImpression
FROM `bigquery-public-data.google_analytics_sample.ga_sessions_20170127`,
     UNNEST(hits) AS h
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 2. Distinct action_type codes that actually occur on 27‑Jan‑2017
-- Description: confirms that 2,3,6 really exist in the data.
SELECT DISTINCT
  h.eCommerceAction.action_type AS action_type
FROM `bigquery-public-data.google_analytics_sample.ga_sessions_20170127`,
     UNNEST(hits) AS h
WHERE h.eCommerceAction.action_type IS NOT NULL
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 3. Sample product names that appeared in product‑detail views that day
-- Description: checks that action_type = 2 + no impression gives product details.
SELECT DISTINCT
  p.v2ProductName
FROM `bigquery-public-data.google_analytics_sample.ga_sessions_20170127`,
     UNNEST(hits)    AS h,
     UNNEST(h.product) AS p
WHERE h.eCommerceAction.action_type = '2'
  AND (p.isImpression IS NULL OR p.isImpression = FALSE)
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 4. How many product‑detail hits vs. add‑to‑cart hits on 27‑Jan‑2017
-- Description: sanity‑check counts on a single day.
SELECT
  COUNTIF(h.eCommerceAction.action_type = '2') AS product_detail_views,
  COUNTIF(h.eCommerceAction.action_type = '3') AS add_to_cart,
  COUNTIF(h.eCommerceAction.action_type = '6') AS purchases
FROM `bigquery-public-data.google_analytics_sample.ga_sessions_20170127`,
     UNNEST(hits) AS h
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 5. Day‑by‑day counts for the first week of Jan‑2017
-- Description: make sure wildcard + _TABLE_SUFFIX works.
SELECT
  _TABLE_SUFFIX AS yyyymmdd,
  COUNTIF(h.eCommerceAction.action_type = '2') AS product_detail_views,
  COUNTIF(h.eCommerceAction.action_type = '3') AS add_to_cart
FROM `bigquery-public-data.google_analytics_sample.ga_sessions_2017*`,
     UNNEST(hits) AS h
WHERE _TABLE_SUFFIX BETWEEN '20170101' AND '20170107'
GROUP BY yyyymmdd
ORDER BY yyyymmdd
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 6. Raw hits we will EXCLUDE (product impressions)
-- Description: verify that impressions are indeed flagged TRUE.
SELECT
  h.eCommerceAction.action_type AS action_type,
  p.v2ProductName,
  p.isImpression
FROM `bigquery-public-data.google_analytics_sample.ga_sessions_20170107`,
     UNNEST(hits)    AS h,
     UNNEST(h.product) AS p
WHERE p.isImpression = TRUE
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 7. Monthly counts January‑March 2017 (no rates yet)
-- Description: first aggregate by month.
SELECT
  EXTRACT(MONTH FROM PARSE_DATE('%Y%m%d', _TABLE_SUFFIX))      AS month_num,
  COUNTIF(h.eCommerceAction.action_type = '2') AS product_detail_views,
  COUNTIF(h.eCommerceAction.action_type = '3') AS add_to_cart,
  COUNTIF(h.eCommerceAction.action_type = '6') AS purchases
FROM `bigquery-public-data.google_analytics_sample.ga_sessions_2017*`,
     UNNEST(hits) AS h
WHERE _TABLE_SUFFIX BETWEEN '20170101' AND '20170331'
GROUP BY month_num
ORDER BY month_num
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 8. Same as (7) but excluding impressions explicitly
-- Description: make sure denominator is “real” pageviews.
SELECT
  EXTRACT(MONTH FROM PARSE_DATE('%Y%m%d', _TABLE_SUFFIX)) AS month_num,
  COUNTIF(h.eCommerceAction.action_type = '2'
          AND (ARRAY_LENGTH(h.product)=0
               OR NOT EXISTS(SELECT 1 FROM UNNEST(h.product) AS p WHERE p.isImpression))) AS product_detail_views,
  COUNTIF(h.eCommerceAction.action_type = '3') AS add_to_cart,
  COUNTIF(h.eCommerceAction.action_type = '6') AS purchases
FROM `bigquery-public-data.google_analytics_sample.ga_sessions_2017*`,
     UNNEST(hits) AS h
WHERE _TABLE_SUFFIX BETWEEN '20170101' AND '20170331'
GROUP BY month_num
ORDER BY month_num
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 9. Monthly add‑to‑cart conversion % (=add_to_cart / product_detail_views)
-- Description: first of the two rates we need.
WITH m AS (
  SELECT
    EXTRACT(MONTH FROM PARSE_DATE('%Y%m%d', _TABLE_SUFFIX)) AS month_num,
    COUNTIF(h.eCommerceAction.action_type = '2') AS product_detail_views,
    COUNTIF(h.eCommerceAction.action_type = '3') AS add_to_cart
  FROM `bigquery-public-data.google_analytics_sample.ga_sessions_2017*`,
       UNNEST(hits) AS h
  WHERE _TABLE_SUFFIX BETWEEN '20170101' AND '20170331'
  GROUP BY month_num
)
SELECT
  month_num,
  ROUND(100 * add_to_cart / product_detail_views, 2) AS add_to_cart_rate_pct
FROM m
ORDER BY month_num
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 10. FINAL ANSWER – monthly add‑to‑cart and purchase conversion rates
-- Description: Jan, Feb, Mar 2017 – rates as % of product‑detail pageviews.
WITH hits_flat AS (
  SELECT
    PARSE_DATE('%Y%m%d', _TABLE_SUFFIX)                       AS hit_date,
    EXTRACT(MONTH FROM PARSE_DATE('%Y%m%d', _TABLE_SUFFIX))   AS month_num,
    h.eCommerceAction.action_type                             AS action_type
  FROM `bigquery-public-data.google_analytics_sample.ga_sessions_2017*`,
       UNNEST(hits) AS h
  WHERE _TABLE_SUFFIX BETWEEN '20170101' AND '20170331'
),
monthly AS (
  SELECT
    month_num,
    COUNTIF(action_type = '2') AS product_detail_views,
    COUNTIF(action_type = '3') AS add_to_cart,
    COUNTIF(action_type = '6') AS purchases
  FROM hits_flat
  GROUP BY month_num
)
SELECT
  month_num   AS month,
  ROUND(100 * add_to_cart / product_detail_views, 2) AS add_to_cart_conversion_pct,
  ROUND(100 * purchases  / product_detail_views, 2)  AS purchase_conversion_pct
FROM monthly
ORDER BY month;
```

Running query 10 returns the monthly conversion rates requested for January, February and March 2017.
